e differential equation ${y}^{″}+5{y}^{′}+6y=0$ represents the equation of damped harmonic motion. \nThe auxiliary equation for $\\lambda $ is\n\n$$\n{\\lambda }^{2}+5\\lambda +6=0\n$$\n\nThe discriminant of this quadratic equation is:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}D={5}^{2}-4(1)(6) & =1>0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus, the given equation represents heavy damping, and so statement I is false.\n\n- The differential equation ${y}^{″}+2{y}^{′}+y=0$ represents the equation of damped harmonic motion. \nThe auxiliary equation for $\\lambda $ is:\n\n$$\n{\\lambda }^{2}+2\\lambda +1=0\n$$\n\nThe discriminant of this quadratic equation is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}D={2}^{2}-4(1)(1) & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus, the given equation represents critical damping, and so statement II is false.\n\n- The differential equation ${y}^{″}+4{y}^{′}+2y=0$ represents the equation of damped harmonic motion. \nThe auxiliary equation for $\\lambda $ is:\n\n$$\n{\\lambda }^{2}+4\\lambda +2=0\n$$\n\nThe discriminant of this quadratic equation is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}D={4}^{2}-4(1)(2) & =8>0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus, the given equation represents heavy damping, and so statement III is correct.\n\nIn conclusion, the correct answer is \"III only\"." 13194139535418 true] [17592186348232 1000 #edb/ref 17592186348233 13194139535418 true] [17592186348232 1000 #edb/ref 17592186348234 13194139535418 true] [17592186348232 1000 #edb/ref 17592186348235 13194139535418 true] [17592186348232 1000 #edb/ref 17592186348236 13194139535418 true] [17592186348232 1000 #edb/ref 17592186348237 13194139535418 true] [17592186348232 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535418 true] [17592186348232 1041 "selection" 13194139535418 true] [17592186348232 1104 #edb/ref 17592186348235 13194139535418 true] [17592186348232 1110 #uuid "905f579c-e17c-5d3c-8636-bb6e705ab18e" 13194139535418 true] [17592186348233 1034 "I and III only" 13194139535418 true] [17592186348233 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535418 true] [17592186348233 1111 #uuid "38255b87-3b9c-5d04-93c4-2306ca713e97" 13194139535418 true] [17592186348234 1034 "I only" 13194139535418 true] [17592186348234 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535418 true] [17592186348234 1111 #uuid "9cdb8920-8478-5970-8954-cc107f5a65fe" 13194139535418 true] [17592186348235 1034 "III only" 13194139535418 true] [17592186348235 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535418 true] [17592186348235 1111 #uuid "d600b204-4097-5140-bff8-9cc5f7e5de00" 13194139535418 true] [17592186348236 1034 "I and II only" 13194139535418 true] [17592186348236 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535418 true] [17592186348236 1111 #uuid "c206a65b-e4d2-5643-b1ca-fc22f849f7de" 13194139535418 true] [17592186348237 1034 "II only" 13194139535418 true] [17592186348237 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535418 true] [17592186348237 1111 #uuid "9427e006-6b12-5911-95d0-c4f1103301e5" 13194139535418 true] [17592186348238 1017 #edb/ref 17592186348239 13194139535418 true] [17592186348238 1089 "q-64623" 13194139535418 true] [17592186348238 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139535418 true] [17592186348238 1100 "The position $y(t)$ of a particle oscillating with light damped harmonic motion is governed by the equation\n\n$$\n{y}^{″}+8{y}^{′}+52y=0,\n$$\n\nwhere $t>0$ is the time, in seconds. What is the period of the damped oscillation?" 13194139535418 true] [17592186348238 1113 #uuid "9e801805-48d7-5f7f-a2eb-42e2eeee70b1" 13194139535418 true] [17592186348238 1145 "The given equation represents the equation of damped harmonic motion. We are looking for solutions of the form $y={e}^{\\lambda t}.$\n\nThe auxiliary equation for $\\lambda $ is\n\n$$\n{\\lambda }^{2}+8\\lambda +52=0.\n$$\n\nThe auxiliary equation can be solved by completing the square:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\lambda }^{2}+8\\lambda +52 & =0 \\\\ ({\\lambda }^{2}+8\\lambda +16)-16+52 & =0 \\\\ (\\lambda +4)^{2}+36 & =0 \\\\ (\\lambda +4)^{2} & =-36 \\\\ \\lambda +4 & =\\pm 6\\text{i} \\\\ \\lambda  & =-4\\pm 6\\text{i}\\end{aligned}\n$